     "assumptions": [
      "There is no existing code, so every requirement is ADDED. Endpoint paths in acceptance criteria only show the contract.",
      "ASM-24 (Stripe card payments) conflicts with request section 32 (no online card payments in this phase). The spec follows the request: staff record payment manually with a payment date and the recording user.",
      "Rejection HTTP status codes differ between drafts (e.g. 400 vs 410 for expired links, 400 vs 422 vs 409 for validation errors, 202 vs 200 for reset requests). d3 states codes are examples; the merged ACs use one code where drafts agree on the outcome, and the fixed rule is success or rejection with no record change on rejection.",
      "The pending invitation status is called \"Pending\" (d1/d2) or \"Invited\" (d3); these are the same state.",
      "An ERP file fails validation as a whole if it is missing, unreadable, empty, missing a required column, or has any non-numeric or negative quantity. Unknown product identifiers alone do not fail the file (ASM-6).",
      "Stock import rows are matched by distributor product code until the client supplies the column layout (ASM-7). Products missing from a valid file keep their previous quantity; a product never imported counts as Out of stock.",
      "Placing or confirming an order does not reduce imported stock; nothing is reserved.",
      "Price or stock changes at checkout reject the submission and return current values; the order is never silently repriced.",
      "Repeat order works for an order of any status and adds lines at their original quantity, capped at available stock and flagged when reduced.",
      "Order and basket totals are net (tax-exclusive); tax and gross appear only on invoices (ASM-9). One currency with 2 decimal places.",
      "A deactivated price list cannot be newly assigned. If a company has no assigned or an inactive price list, every product shows 'Price on request' (d3).",
      "Search is a case-insensitive substring match; ranking is not specified.",
      "Vehicle compatibility entries store a model-year range (from–to) (d1); d3 says model year.",
      "Confirmation validation means every line is active and within available stock and the delivery address still exists.",
      "A password reset request returns the same response whether or not the email exists.",
